on-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Mausoleum of Emperor Ferdinand II was built from 1614 until 1638 by Ferdinand's Italian court painter and architect. On the gable stands a statue of St. Catherine of Alexandria. The statue is facing the former Jesuit college. This is very fitting as St. Catherine is the patron saint of universities. Behind and to the right of the gable is a gold eagle perched on a globe. This symbolizes the Emperor's power and position on top of the world.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/DSC_0477.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The former Jesuit college is located across from Emperor Ferdinand&#039;s mausoleum. In 1585 Graz University was founded and today, it&#039;s the Seminary.\n&lt;p&gt; In 2005, Manfred Erjautz created a sculpture entitled &lt;i&gt;Searching for Permanence&lt;\/i&gt;. The sculpture emphasizes that nothing lasts forever. The clock at the top of the building reflects in the artificial puddle in front of the snowman forcing him to watch the passage of time as he stands still.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"620\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The former Jesuit college is located across from Emperor Ferdinand&#039;s mausoleum. In 1585 Graz University was founded and today, it&#039;s the Seminary.\n&lt;p&gt; In 2005, Manfred Erjautz created a sculpture entitled &lt;i&gt;Searching for Permanence&lt;\/i&gt;. The sculpture emphasizes that nothing lasts forever. The clock at the top of the building reflects in the artificial puddle in front of the snowman forcing him to watch the passage of time as he stands still.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/DSC_0477\/1401934786.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The former Jesuit college is located across from Emperor Ferdinand's mausoleum. In 1585 Graz University was founded and today, it's the Seminary.\n<p> In 2005, Manfred Erjautz created a sculpture entitled <i>Searching for Permanence<\/i>. The sculpture emphasizes that nothing lasts forever. The clock at the top of the building reflects in the artificial puddle in front of the snowman forcing him to watch the passage of time as he stands still.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/DSC_0481.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The facade of a boarding for the wealthier students of the Jesuit college. It was rather luxurious as each of the guests had their personal servant.\" data-attachment-id=\"621\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The facade of a boarding for the wealthier students of the Jesuit college. It was rather luxurious as each of the guests had their personal servant.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/DSC_0481\/2609264307.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div c